1. Cover A on the signed title: lab/experiments/33-designer-cover-studies/cover-a-signed.svg, the full Crown Quarto front (189 x 246.1 mm, its size stated), before the title page in both editions, full bleed.
2. The on-stage marker in place of each page's cast-bar line: lab/characters/editions/marker-<edition>-<page>.svg, one per page file that has a cast bar (03/01 to 03/03, 10/01 to 10/09), 87 mm wide, no text inside; the narrator's head first, then the nine in the order they came on stage, the present lit (read from the cast-bar words, and from C011's first commits where the words give a time). The cast-bar sentence can stay under it as the caption.
3. The speakers' heads: lab/tools/book/speakers.css, a fragment to add after lab-look.css; it puts a 6 mm head before each .speaker block by data-speaker, with the mood's face when data-mood is happy, worried, stressed or unhappy (other stage words get the happy face). Tested on a scratch copy of your 10-page build: 11 pages, no change in page count.
All three are rebuilt from the manuscript by python3 lab/characters/editions.py and lab/experiments/33-designer-cover-studies/make_covers.py, so a changed cast bar means one rerun. The four scorecards and a picture of the factory's stations for the dashed figures come next round.

